suite, all three harnesses AND the configured suite before handoff — the first attempt at this leaf failed construction on eight of its own tests, so treat construction as the last check, never the first.\n10|Procedure: this is the FINAL leaf, so internal/traceability is yours — the registry is the adopted `ownership.v0.7.0.json`, the pin must be re-derived from the registry as it stands in your candidate, and the README measured-coverage subsection must equal what tracecheck prints on your tree and still pass the landed `readme_coverage_pin_test.go`. The reviewer confirms those are currently correct, so do not disturb them beyond what item 4 requires. Your Story branch descends from c3aae73; do not refresh unless origin/main actually moves — and note that the sibling Story STORY-260830-1cyj0q may land first, in which case origin/main WILL move and you must then run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-2056mm`, audit every path in `git diff --name-only c3aae73 <new base>` that also appears in your `git status`, keep README and LOGBOOK edits additive on the NEW content, and MERGE the ownership registry rather than replacing it. Never commit on the Story branch, never edit `.task-board` directly, never self-accept. Update the results with a finding-by-finding table (finding -> change -> the test that fails without it -> evidence path), update the conformance matrix and the evidence archive (a real gzip archive, one raw log per plant with its subprocess exit, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1), re-complete the checklist, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-2056mm --role developer` so revision 3 is constructed, and exit promptly. Hand off no later than 2.5 hours in. Report the ratio you MEASURE.\n11|PARTIAL-ATTEMPT RECOVERY: if a previous attempt died mid-way, the Story worktree still carries its partial edits — start with `git -C .temp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree status --short` and `git diff`, state what you inherited, and verify it against this brief instead 