ng anything, because several of those names suggest the refusal tables and the evidence resolver disagree with each other rather than with the spec.\n25|The discipline point, because it cost an hour and a full 30-command suite: run your own package's tests (`go test ./internal/termbind -count=1 -v`) and then the repository suite BEFORE handoff. Change Request construction is not your first test run — by the time the runtime rejects a revision, a reviewer slot and a suite have already been spent, and the revision number is burned whether or not anyone read the code.\n26|Everything you already wrote in the worktree is preserved: start with `git -C .temp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree status --short` and `git diff`, state in your results what you inherited, fix the eight failures, and only then hand off. Your scope is otherwise unchanged.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3c3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3fc-2962-7bc0-91c2-787ae4899fa1"},"sequence":60,"recorded_at":1780531400000115,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a"},"call_id":"call_01a0b3fc5de37329b95695032b6f301d","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-2056mm/TASK-260830-2056mm_rework-rev3.md`.\n1|THIS BRIEF SUPERSEDES EVERY EARLIER PRECONDITION ON TASK-260830-2056mm, including TASK-260830-2056mm_producer.md (still the scope of record for WHAT the leaf owns, but its execution instructions are replaced by this one). Do exactly what is written here.\n2|Rework run for TASK-260830-2056mm, the FINAL leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe. The story_final Change Request revision 2 was reviewed by RUN-260918-acd5a8 (claude-opus-5 max) and routed CHANGES REQUESTED: NO P1, one P2 class and five P3. Read TASK-260830-2056mm_review-verdict-rev2.md and TASK-260830-2056mm_review-evidence-rev2.tar.gz first. The reviewer confirms on its own instruments that the Change Request is otherwise sound: both v4 payloads are member-for-member the pinned text and validated at the append boundary by the landed canonical owner, evidence resolution and identity refusal hold on every surface, lost-create recovery holds with a real SIGKILL seam, takeover and attach authority hold, and the registry re-pin, the re-derived digest, tracecheck and the README figures are all correct. Keep every bit of that.\n3|The P2 is the one closed-object parser this Story owns, the Section 4.B Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0, and it is the class your own brief listed under (c): never fork canonicaljson or the AX number model. `ParseTerminalBinding` admits two members the pinned table refuses, and through one of them it reaches the FORKED omit-self identity rule, which then accepts JSON numbers and nested duplicate members that the landed identity rule refuses. Worth saying plainly: the other Story's final leaf was rejected in the same hour for the same class at a different member — one repository-wide rule, several local re-implementations, each weaker than the original. Fix it at the parser, not at the two witnessed members:\n4|1. `ParseTerminalBinding` must enforce `protocol_version` major 1 and `extensions == {}` per Section 4.B; `bindingIdentity` must refuse JSON numbers at ANY depth and nested duplicate members BEFORE the JCS transform — preferably by reusing the landed `terminalbackend` rule rather than growing another copy. Drive EVERY member arm of the Binding table negatively through the production entry (the reviewer measured the committed suite executing 7 of 30 arms), ship narrowing rows for the new arms and for `supersedes_binding_id`, and re-run the landed-agreement test with a numeric extension value.\n5|2. Commit `TestRV2W_RecoverGenerationBoundBeforeStatusRead` (or an equivalent) with its harness row.\n6|3. `EmitResumed`: compose `sessprofile.CheckResumedPair` plus a known-checkpoint check, or state the bound explicitly — do not leave it implied.\n7|4. Correct the prose so it states what the tree does: the harness notes for the two pre-scan rows, LOGBOOK F2 (append a correction rather than rewriting history), the README sentence about the \"pinned protocol class … bootstrap binding\", `resolve.go`'s \"every failure\", row 57 / 5.2#18 as a bound, and the 7.A citation.\n8|5. Record in the results and the LOGBOOK the restore/terminate-stale follow-up owner and the `HandoffFailed` non-applicability.\n9|6. Re-run your own package suite, all three harnesses AND the configured suite before handoff — the first attempt at this leaf failed construction on eight of its own tests, so treat construction as the last check, never the first.\n10|Procedure: this is the FINAL leaf, so internal/traceability is yours — the registry is the adopted `ownership.v0.7.0.json`, the pin must be re-derived from the registry as it stands in your candidate, and the README measured-coverage subsection must equal what tracecheck prints on your tree and still pass the landed `readme_coverage_pin_test.go`. The reviewer confirms those are currently correct, so do not disturb them beyond what item 4 requires. Your Story branch descends from c3aae73; do not refresh unless origin/main actually moves — and note that the sibling Story STORY-260830-1cyj0q may land first, in which case origin/main WILL move and you must then run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-2056mm`, audit every path in `git diff --name-only c3aae73 <new base>` that also appears in your `git status`, keep README and LOGBOOK edits additive on the NEW content, and MERGE the ownership registry rather than replacing it. Never commit on the Story branch, never edit `.task-board` directly, never self-accept. Update the results with a finding-by-finding table (finding -> change -> the test that fails without it -> evidence path), update the conformance matrix and the evidence archive (a real gzip archive, one raw log per plant with its subprocess exit, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1), re-complete the checklist, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-2056mm --role developer` so revision 3 is constructed, and exit promptly. Hand off no later than 2.5 hours in. Report the ratio you MEASURE.\n11|PARTIAL-ATTEMPT RECOVERY: if a previous attempt died mid-way, the Story worktree still carries its partial edits — start with `git -C .temp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree status --short` and `git diff`, state what you inherited, and verify it against this brief instead of assuming it is correct.\n12|Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The same claude-opus-5 max reviewer contract applies to revision 3.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
