{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c41f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3fc-2962-7bc0-91c2-787ae4899fa1"},"sequence":106,"recorded_at":1780531400000207,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b3fc-7c59-7903-a33f-a6b0f60f8676"},"task_id":"01a0b3fc-7c59-7903-a33f-a6b0f60f8676","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b3fc-7c59-7903-a33f-a6b0f60f8676","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-2056mm/TASK-260830-2056mm_reviewer-cr2.md`.\n1|Independently review Change Request revision 2 of TASK-260830-2056mm (implement-terminal-binding-events-and-recovery, the FINAL leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe ax-pane-and-terminal-instance-binding — story_final, so the Change Request carries the WHOLE Story: story_final on trunk base c3aae73 with the checkpointed predecessor commits ca1c1d9 c61fc06  on the Story branch (tip ca1c1d9fd640f8c39827c134db13cfbe45373b22), published by RUN-260918-2c22a5 on muse-spark max, 89 changed paths in the whole-Story patch, patch and validation log attached as TASK-260830-2056mm_change-request_rev2.patch / _rev2-validation.log). Read the producer brief TASK-260830-2056mm_producer.md, the outcome TASK-260830-2056mm_results.md, TASK-260830-2056mm_conformance-matrix.md, TASK-260830-2056mm_producer-evidence.tar.gz, the predecessor leaf's accepted evidence (TASK-260830-kkh1an_results.md and its verdict TASK-260830-kkh1an_review-verdict-rev4.md, accepted by RUN-TBD-kkh1an-reviewer), the CR patch and validation log, and the exact immutable CR bytes. The normative authority is the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md Sections 5.2 (Session Event 4.0.0 Terminal Instance events), 4.B, 4.D, 7.A and 13.1. The landed owners are internal/axpane (the wrapper decision core and its durable bootstrap binding, first leaf), internal/terminalbackend (the Section 4.C lifecycle contract, second leaf), internal/sessrepo and internal/sessstate (the event chain and its fold) and internal/fencing.\n2|\n3|Verify with your own instruments. (0) Inherited advisories and the predecessor's verdict — this is the FINAL leaf, so it inherits whatever the review of the previous leaf recorded for its successors. Read the predecessor verdict named in the header above and list every advisory or deferred item it left for this leaf; for each one, grade it closed (naming the committed test that fails without it), explicitly deferred (with the owner and reason recorded in the results), or SILENTLY DROPPED — and treat the third as a finding. The producer brief required a recorded decision for each, and a sibling leaf on the other Story was rejected this session for exactly this: three inherited advisories neither closed nor mentioned, one of which was a live gap pointed at that leaf's own entry point. Do not accept a results section that simply omits them. (1) The two v4 payloads, member for member, extracted by you from the pinned text and diffed against the candidate: `terminal.created` = terminal_binding_id, terminal_backend_id, implementation_version, protocol_version, evidence_ids[1..256] sorted unique; `session.resumed` = checkpoint_id, execution_profile, profile_source_event_id|null and the same five binding members. Session Event 4.0.0 keeps the exact v3 top-level shape, digest rules, lease ordering, predecessor rules and the whole v1-v3 registry — every other payload must be byte-for-byte the v3 definition, so diff them rather than trusting the claim. Witness both array bounds (1 and 256, plus 0 and 257) and an unsorted and a duplicated evidence_ids array. (2) Evidence resolution — evidence_ids MUST resolve locally to validated sanitized Manifest, Probe and applicable Capability Evidence bound to the EVENT's backend id and versions; plant an id that resolves to a native reference, a generation string, a socket, a pipe, an endpoint, a token, a credential, terminal output, a PID or any live-process fact and confirm each refuses. The binding digest is an opaque audit reference: prove no binding object, native_reference or generation string can be reached through the event. (3) Identity refusal — drive all eight forbidden forms (PID, handle, socket, path, named pipe, URL, token, mutable endpoint) as `terminal_instance_id` in the Binding, the Provider Protocol 3 descriptor, the operation bodies and the CLI Result 4 summary, and pair the census with the driven refusals. (4) Lost-result recovery by bootstrap operation ID — kill between effect and result and confirm `status` plus the durable (session_id, bootstrap_operation_id) binding proves absence or identifies the ONE child, never a second child and never a claim of `absent` when the effect cannot be disproven. Drive a duplicate retry with the same operation and a retry with a changed operation both inside and outside the bootstrap window. Note that the predecessor leaf was rejected once for exactly this class: its receipt kept its idempotency key forever, making the table's own recovery column unimplementable — check the row this leaf writes is actually reachable. (5) Version skew and authority — a valid takeover or owner resume MAY select a different admitted backend and emits a NEW binding digest and a new v4 event, never mutating an earlier one and never cloning the session; attach or presentation-client activity emits NEITHER event and changes no Owner/Replica, lease or fencing state (drive an attach and assert zero events and zero state change); a v1-v3 reader keeps a v4 event as inert immutable history and MUST NOT derive runtime state from it or write a lower-version event — drive both directions through the landed sessstate and sessquery readers. (