{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5bb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3fc-2962-7bc0-91c2-787ae4899fa1"},"sequence":312,"recorded_at":1780531400000619,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b3fc-ee62-7cd1-8f4f-71b5db93a2dc"},"task_id":"01a0b3fc-ee62-7cd1-8f4f-71b5db93a2dc","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b3fc-ee62-7cd1-8f4f-71b5db93a2dc","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/tb2056/verdict-rev2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2056mm — independent review verdict, CR-TASK-260830-2056mm-2 revision 2\n2|\n3|**Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED (routed `to-dev`).** One P2 class, five P3.\n4|No P1. The story-final Change Request is otherwise sound on my own\n5|instruments: the two v4 payloads are member-for-member the pinned text and\n6|are validated at the append boundary by the landed canonical owner; evidence\n7|resolution, identity refusal on every surface, lost-create recovery (with a\n8|real SIGKILL seam), takeover/attach authority, the registry re-pin, the\n9|re-derived digest, tracecheck and the README figures all hold. The P2 is\n10|the one closed-object parser this Story owns — the Section 4.B Terminal\n11|Instance Binding 1.0.0 — which admits two members the pinned table refuses\n12|and, through one of them, reaches the forked omit-self identity rule with\n13|JSON numbers and nested duplicate members that the landed identity rule\n14|refuses. That is exactly the \"never fork canonicaljson / the AX number\n15|model\" class the producer brief listed under (c), and the parser's\n16|member-grammar arms are executed 7 of 30 by the committed suite.\n17|\n18|Reviewer: RUN-260918-acd5a8 (claude-opus-5 max). Reviewed bytes: base\n19|`c3aae73df906df1b5aa962c7bc3c16437dd920fa` (= `origin/main`, fetched),\n20|candidate tree `f8adb1616ce3d5e702e50e47ad5795859f4f12d5` (recomputed from\n21|the live Story worktree through a temporary untracked-aware index: equal),\n22|patch sha256 `1e4b15dde201f1c7f3a3169eb985d92e867877828fffe1d383babd451c4b7684`\n23|(equal to the CR record), 89 changed paths, 0 outside the Story's scope\n24|(`logs/00-identity.log`). Every probe ran in isolated `git archive` copies of\n25|the exact tree under `.temp/TASK-260830-2056mm/review-rev2/` (`cand/`\n26|tree-exact checks, `cand-h/` shipped harnesses, `cand-m/` reviewer mutants,\n27|`cand-p/` probes); `cand-h` is byte-identical to the candidate after all six\n28|harness passes and `cand-m` after both mutant passes. The live Story\n29|worktree, index, branch and HEAD were never touched (`git status` is the\n30|same 18-path list at the end as at the start; tree OID unchanged).\n31|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` everywhere, 0 `__pycache__`/`.pyc` in any copy.\n32|Every instrument, raw log and subprocess exit is in\n33|`TASK-260830-2056mm_review-evidence-rev2.tar.gz` (paths below are relative\n34|to that archive).\n35|\n36|## 0. Inherited advisories (final leaf)\n37|\n38|| Item | Where it landed | Grade |\n39|| --- | --- | --- |\n40|| 1geqhj rev4 P3-1 journal-only restore closure | `TestRunJournalOnlyRestoreClosureFromNewest` (axpane `leafclose_test.go`), row `N-journal-closure` KILLED ×2 in my reruns | Closed |\n41|| 1geqhj rev4 P3-2 pure `Decide` on a missing closure | axpane TRACEABILITY story-close section: owner-stated bound (unreachable from every `Run` path) | Explicitly deferred |\n42|| 1geqhj rev4 P3-3 remote owner, newest absent locally | axpane TRACEABILITY story-close section: fail-closed bound, deferred load is future work | Explicitly deferred |\n43|| 1geqhj rev4 P3-4 `EmitParked` winner binding | production fix `events.go` (`decision.WinningLeaseID == params.LeaseID`), `TestEmitParkedWinningLeaseMismatchRefuses`, row `N-parked-winner` KILLED ×2 | Closed |\n44|| 1geqhj rev4 P3-5 corrupt checkpoint blob is not absence | `TestRunCorruptCheckpointBlobIsNotAbsence`, row `N-ckpt-corrupt` KILLED ×2 | Closed |\n45|| 1geqhj rev4 P3-6 reattach carries two instance IDs | closed by kkh1an (documented authority on reattach); nothing left for this leaf | Closed (predecessor) |\n46|| 1geqhj rev4 P3-7 archive hygiene | this leaf's two archives are task-scoped, gzip, 0 pycache, no foreign-task artefacts (`logs/80`) | Closed |\n47|| kkh1an rev4 P3-1 expiry recheck at the third position | `TestRV4W_ExpiryRecheckedBeforeThirdEffect`, row `N-engine-recheck-auth-expiry-third` KILLED ×2 | Closed |\n48|| kkh1an rev4 P3-2 replay-site generation binding / corrupt image | `TestRV4W_ReplayedImageGenerationBindingAtEngine`, `TestRV4_CorruptCompletionImageIsIntegrityFailure`, rows `N-resume-checkresult-stale`, `N-resume-checkresult-disposition`, `N-resume-corrupt-image` KILLED ×2 | Closed |\n49|| kkh1an rev4 P3-3 in-loop deadline instant | `TestRV4W_LoopDeadlineInstantCancelsWaiting`, row `N-engine-loop-deadline-instant` KILLED ×2 | Closed |\n50|| kkh1an rev4 P3-4 mixed-case enum siblings | `TestRV4W_AuthorizationKindCaseSiblingRefused` + three corpora, row `N-auth-kind-case` KILLED ×2 | Closed |\n51|| kkh1an rev4 note: `HandoffFailed` member if the final leaf wires a reporter | this leaf wires no `HandoffFailed` reporter (grep: only tests set it), so not applicable — but the results do not say so | Not applicable, unrecorded (P3-5) |\n52|| kkh1an rev3 P3-5 / kkh1an doc: restore and terminate-stale execution \"belongs to the story's final leaf\" | termbind TRACEABILITY: \"remains refused by the terminstance scope gates (owner: terminstance)\" — the two leaves point at each other and neither brief assigned it | Deferred with a circular owner (P3-5) |\n53|\n54|All eight closures executed on the exact tree (`logs/60-leafclose-witnesses.log`: 8 PASS).\n55|\n56|## 1. What holds (verified myself on the exact tree)\n57|\n58|| Check | Result | Evidence |\n59|| --- | --- | --- |\n60|| gofmt (empty list) / `go build ./...` / `go vet ./...`; `GOOS=linux` and `GOOS=windows` builds; `GOOS=windows go vet` termbind; JSON validity; `git diff --check base..candidate`; `cataloggen -adopted -check` | all exit 0 | `logs/02`, `logs/80` |\n61|| `go test ./... -count=1` on the exact tree | 41/41 packages `ok` (40 in the first run; `internal/specpin` failed only because I had stripped `.task-board` from the copy and passed once restored) | `logs/04`, `logs/04b` |\n62|| `go test ./... -race -count=1` (Story packages + the other 34 packages, two bounded calls) | 41/41 `ok`, 0 `DATA RACE` — the rev1 race is gone | `logs/70`, `logs/71` |\n63|| `go test ./internal/termbind -count=1 -v` | 187 PASS lines, 0 FAIL, 0 SKIP; `-cover` 76.9% | `logs/83`, `logs/termbind.coverprofile` |\n64|| CR construction suite | runtime-recorded `required=30 green=30 failed=0 missing=0` on the exact tree (accepted from the attached bounded `_rev2-validation.log`; the 17 fuzz gates and `task-board validate` were not rerun by me) | resource |\n65|| Payloads vs the pinned text (`SPEC.v0.7.0.md` 1956–1985): `terminal.created` = terminal_binding_id, terminal_backend_id, implementation_version, protocol_version, evidence_ids[1..256]; `session.resumed` = checkpoint_id, execution_profile, profile_source_event_id\\|null + the same five — identical to `axpane.TerminalCreatedPayload`/`ResumedPayload` and to the landed `canonicaljson` 4.0.0 registry (`core_records.go:574-575`, `validateTerminalV4Payload`), which is composed at the append boundary by `axpane.Emit → sessrepo.AppendEvent → VerifyObjectIdentity` | holds | source read |\n66|| Bounds at the append boundary: 256 and 1 admit, 257 and 0 refuse (`member evidence_ids exceeds maximum length 256` / `requires at least 1 entries`); unsorted and duplicated sets refuse at `ResolveEvidence` and at the emission entries | holds | `TestRV2_AppendBoundaryEvidenceBounds` `logs/15`; producer rows 17–20, 29 |\n67|| Evidence resolution: eleven foreign kinds, unresolvable ID, substitution under another ID, foreign backend / protocol drift, landed admission faults (claim, forgery, expiry, drift) all refuse the mismatch class; nil registry fails closed (`terminal_backend_not_found at registry unavailable`), never panics; the event bytes carry the opaque digest and no native reference, generation, or instance ID | holds | producer rows 16–26, 34; `TestRV2_ResolveEvidenceNilRegistry` `logs/14` |\n68|| Identity: eight forbidden forms refuse at `CheckInstanceIdentity`, `ParseTerminalBinding`, the landed `AdmitProviderDescriptor`, the operation-body wrappers, `axpane.Store.Bind` (plain error, nothing persisted) and `AttachStore.Attach`; the story gate (`scalar.ParseUUIDv7`) agrees with the landed body authority (`environ.CheckUUIDv7`) on a 15-spelling corpus (upper-case, v4, wrong variants, `urn:uuid:`, braces, NUL, 35/37 chars): 0 disagreements | holds | `TestRV2_IdentityGateAgreesWithLandedUUIDv7` `logs/12` |\n69|| Recovery: real SIGKILL between the durable bind + effect and the result → the ONE child; duplicate retry same verdict; changed op in the fold-derived open window → `idempotency_mismatch`, outside it proceeds; five unprovable shapes → `unavailable`/`status_first`, never absence; status read failure is an error. My narrowings on the two arms the producer did not mutate — absence claimed without the identity match (`RV2-M7`), backend-`unavailable` reported as the child (`RV2-M8`) — KILLED ×2 by `TestRecoverCreateNeverClaimsAbsent` | holds | `logs/50`, `logs/51` |\n70|| Authority: emission under a losing epoch, under a REMOTE winner (presented = winner, local host not the holder → `not_owner`) and under unverified ownership refuses with zero appends (composition of `fencing.AuthorizeMutation` through `axpane.Emit`); takeover selects the conpty backend with a new digest and a new v4 event, the first event's bytes unchanged, one Logical Session, no fork; attach emits nothing and takes no repository | holds | `TestRV2_EmitUnderRemoteWinnerRefuses` `logs/14`; producer rows 32, 51, 54 |\n71|| Story close: the ADOPTED `ownership.v0.7.0.json` is edited (trunk rows merged, four bindings upgraded, `section:4.1` added with the mirrored `storyNewV070Bindings` literal list); `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` re-derived by me from the registry as it stands: `89944b8c6ec75703c0e07432890182ebbb9bb405f28502b05a6632662cebee9b` (canonical bytes 166083) = the pin; `tracecheck` green with exactly `contracts=64 normative_sections=36 acceptance_cases=147 fixtures=33 compatibility_contracts=55 assigned_scopes=0` / `bindings=69 full=2 partial=9 sliver=9 unevidenced=45 unmeasured=4 unowned=7 clauses_discharged=63/574`; section runs 4.1 → 1/5 sliver, 4.B → 1/12 sliver, 4.D → 1/3 sliver, 5.2 → 3/18 sliver, 7.A → 1/2 partial (each exit 1 by design); every clause line/excerpt re-read verbatim in the pinned document; `TestREADMEMeasuredCoverageMatchesTracecheckReport` executed and PASS; README figures equal the printed report; README and LOGBOOK purely additive on the c3aae73 content (README removes only the superseded coverage-figure lines) | holds | `logs/24`, `25`, `26`, `27` |\n72|| Bounds and hygiene: `task-board.config.json` byte-identical to trunk; the only trunk-moved paths (2fc6d50..c3aae73) in the candidate delta are README/LOGBOOK (additive) and the traceability files (edited on top of c3aae73); 0 `__pycache__`/`.pyc`; both producer archives are real gzip, task-scoped, carry `cmd01..cmd30` (cmd05 in 8 chunks, 0 `DATA RACE`), 30+30 raw per-plant termbind logs, blob OIDs before/after, no foreign-task artefacts | holds | `logs/80` |\n73|| Shipped harnesses, isolated pristine copy, two full passes each with raw per-plant output and subprocess exits | termbind 30/30 ×2 (28 narrowing + 1 labelled arm-delete KILLED, `C-control` SURVIVED); axpane 56/56 ×2; terminstance 122/122 ×2; verdict lists identical across passes; copy byte-identical afterwards | `logs/harness/*-pass{1,2}-verdicts.log`, `*-verbose.log` |\n74|\n75|## 2. Coverage statement\n76|\n77|Producer claim: 60 of 60 rows driven. Re-derived (`logs/82-ratio-check.log`):\n78|60 numbered rows (1..60, contiguous, unique); 53 distinct cited top-level\n79|tests = the package's whole `go test -list`, every one PASS in my verbose\n80|run. **I measure 59 of 60 driven at the named entry.** Row 57 (\"v4 carries\n81|no v1 derivation member: a v1 reader stays inert\") is a payload-member\n82|census — no v1-v3-only reader exists on trunk, the landed `sessstate`\n83|reader is v4-aware — so it is a stated bound wearing a driven row's clothes\n84|(P3-4a). Rows 11 and 12 are driven, but at wrapper entries no production\n85|path calls, and their refusal is the landed parsers' (P3-1). Rows 3–8 hide\n86|the real gap: the Binding parser's member-grammar arms (P2-1).\n87|\n88|## 3. Findings\n89|\n90|### P2-1 — `ParseTerminalBinding` admits two members the pinned §4.B Binding table refuses, and through one of them the forked identity rule launders JSON numbers and nested duplicates (production; class: closed-shape rule unenforced + landed-gate fork, producer-brief patterns (c) and (f))\n91|\n92|Pinned text (`SPEC.v0.7.0.md` 1058–1073): `protocol_version` = \"semver in\n93|Terminal Backend Protocol major 1, equal to the Probe\"; `extensions` =\n94|\"exact empty object `{}`\". Both are decidable from the document alone and\n95|the landed owners enforce both on their own objects (`CheckVersionTuple`\n96|refuses `protocol_version major 1`; `terminalbackend.checkExtensions`\n97|admits exactly `{}`). The candidate's parser (`identity.go:183`,\n98|`identity.go:222`) checks `environ.CheckSemver` only and\n99|`environ.CheckExtensions`, which admits any reverse-DNS-keyed object with\n100|arbitrary values.\n101|\n102|Executed (`probes/zz_review2_probe_test.go`, `logs/12-probes-all-pass{1,2}.log`,\n103|identical across passes):\n104|\n105|- `TestRV2_BindingProtocolVersionMajorOne`: `protocol_version` `2.0.0`,\n106|  `0.9.0`, `3.1.4` are **ADMITTED** (parsed binding returned). Control: the\n107|  landed `CheckVersionTuple` refuses `2.0.0` with\n108|  `terminal_backend_implementation_drift … protocol_version major 1`\n109|  (`TestRV2_LandedTupleRefusesNonMajorOne`). Reviewer mutant\n110|  `RV2-M3` (admit exactly `2.0.0` past the semver arm) SURVIVED ×2 because\n111|  it is equivalent to the shipped code: no major-1 arm exists to narrow.\n112|- `TestRV2_BindingExtensionsMustBeEmptyObject`:\n113|  `\"extensions\":{\"com.example.note\":\"y\"}` is **ADMITTED**.\n114|- `TestRV2_BindingIdentityLaundersNumbers` (4 subtests): with the\n115|  `binding_id` computed the way the candidate's own `bindingIdentity`\n116|  computes it, `{\"com.example.n\":1.0}`, `9007199254740993`, `1e2` and `-0`\n117|  in `extensions` are all **ADMITTED** — `bindingIdentity` decodes to\n118|  `map[string]any` (float64), re-marshals, then JCS-transforms, so the\n119|  digest is taken over a rounded/reformatted document. The landed\n120|  `terminalbackend.objectIdentity` walks the document with\n121|  `refuseIdentityNumbers` before the transform (NUM-UNSAFE-NUMBER); the\n122|  fork has no walk. The doc comment on `bindingIdentity` (\"Every member is\n123|  type-checked before this runs, so no JSON number can reach the digest\n124|  bytes\") is false as shipped: extension values are not type-checked.\n125|- `TestRV2_BindingExtensionNestedShapes/nested_duplicate_member`:\n126|  `{\"com.example.o\":{\"a\":\"1\",\"a\":\"2\"}}` is **ADMITTED** (`json.Decoder`\n127|  keeps the last duplicate; the strict frame decoder guards the top level\n128|  only). Lone surrogates are refused by the frame decoder — that half is\n129|  fine.\n130|- The parser's refusal arms are executed 7 of 30 by the committed suite\n131|  (`logs/82-ratio-check.log` and the coverprofile census in\n132|  `logs/termbind.coverprofile`): schema_version, binding_id digest,\n133|  session/host/incarnation UUIDv7, terminal_backend_id, implementation\n134|  semver, protocol semver, created_at, the whole non-null\n135|  `supersedes_binding_id` path and the extensions arm are never reached.\n136|  Reviewer mutant `RV2-M5` (admit exactly `\"not-a-digest\"` as\n137|  `supersedes_binding_id`) SURVIVED ×2 with a non-equivalent witness\n138|  `TestRV2W_SupersedesMustBeDigest` (PASS pristine, FAIL ×2 under the\n139|  plant; `logs/53`).\n140|\n141|Why P2 and not P1: the Binding is host-local, AX-authored and never\n142|replicated, so the over-admission produces a stored document with junk\n143|extensions or a foreign protocol major, not an unsafe launch or\n144|authorization. Why not P3: it is the one new closed-object parser this\n145|Story owns, two rows of its pinned table are unenforced, the identity rule\n146|is a fork of exactly the class the brief named, and the matrix's rows 3–8\n147|present the parser as measured while 23 of its 30 arms are not.\n148|\n149|Fix (for the producer): add the two arms delegating to the landed\n150|authorities (`semverMajor(protocol) == 1` as `CheckVersionTuple` does;\n151|extensions exactly `{}` as the landed manifest/probe/evidence parsers do),\n152|make `bindingIdentity` refuse any JSON number before the transform (mirror\n153|`refuseIdentityNumbers`, or export the landed rule from `terminalbackend`\n154|and call it) and refuse nested duplicate members, then drive every member\n155|arm of the table with a negative through `ParseTerminalBinding` and ship a\n156|narrowing row per arm (major-1 admitted for one value, one non-empty\n157|extensions object admitted, one number admitted, `supersedes` one\n158|non-digest admitted). Re-run `TestBindingIdentityAgreesWithLandedAdmission`\n159|with a numeric extension value so the agreement claim covers the number\n160|model.\n161|\n162|### P3-1 — The operation-body pre-scans add no refusal class; their mutant rows are killed by a Go error type, and the LOGBOOK/harness notes state the opposite (evidence + prose)\n163|\n164|`terminstance.ParseMutationContext` and `ParseStatusBody` already refuse\n165|every non-UUIDv7 `terminal_instance_id` with the pinned wire code\n166|`terminal_backend_protocol_error` (`context.go:78`, `status.go:126`;\n167|`TestRV2_LandedBodyParsersAlreadyRefusePinnedCode`: 16/16 forms, code\n168|`terminal_backend_protocol_error`, type `*terminstance.Error`). The termbind\n169|wrappers `AdmitMutationContext`/`AdmitStatusBody` re-run the same rule and\n170|return the same code as a `*terminalbackend.Error`. Rows `N-prescan-context`\n171|and `N-status-prescan` are KILLED only because `requireCode` asserts the\n172|Go type `*terminalbackend.Error`; with the pre-scan gone, production still\n173|refuses the PID with the pinned code. The harness notes (\"the landed plain\n174|refusal surfaces instead of the pinned code\") and LOGBOOK F2 (\"the\n175|mutation-context/status/bootstrap surfaces needed one (landed plain\n176|refusals)\") are factually wrong for the two body surfaces, and no wrapper\n177|exists for the bootstrap surface at all (row 14 drives the landed\n178|`Store.Bind`, whose refusal is a plain uncoded error — the README sentence\n179|\"with the pinned protocol class on … the bootstrap binding\" outruns it).\n180|No production caller uses either wrapper (grep: tests only). Either drop\n181|the wrappers and name the landed parsers as rows 11/12's call sites, or\n182|keep them as a documented redundancy with the notes corrected; append a\n183|LOGBOOK correction paragraph (the log is append-only).\n184|\n185|### P3-2 — `EmitResumed` binds neither `checkpoint_id` to the chain nor the profile pair to the referenced checkpoint's closure (production characterization; same shape as 1geqhj P3-4)\n186|\n187|`TestRV2_ResumedCheckpointNotBoundToChain` (`logs/14`): a never-published\n188|digest with `execution_profile: yolo` and a null source appends through\n189|`EmitResumed`, and the landed fold then reports that digest as the newest\n190|checkpoint (`HasCheckpoint=true`, `Newest=sha256:fafa…`). The landed\n191|`sessprofile.CheckResumedPair` (\"binds one observed session.resumed pair to\n192|the effective pair of its referenced checkpoint's own closure\") has zero\n193|production callers. Through the wrapper's decision both values would come\n194|from the fold; a direct caller can author a lying newest. Compose the\n195|landed check (derive the want over the referenced checkpoint's heads) and\n196|require the checkpoint to be one the chain/store knows, or state the bound\n197|in `emit.go` and TRACEABILITY in those words.\n198|\n199|### P3-3 — Unmeasured arm found by narrowing: the recovery generation bound (evidence)\n200|\n201|`RV2-M9` (`recover.go`: skip `GenerationDigest` exactly for a 257-character\n202|generation before the status read) SURVIVED ×2; witness\n203|`TestRV2W_RecoverGenerationBoundBeforeStatusRead` (PASS pristine:\n204|`terminal_backend_stale_generation at backend_generation bound` with zero\n205|status reads; FAIL ×2 under the plant: the read runs). Commit the witness\n206|and a row. (`RV2-M6`, the manifest implementation-version arm of\n207|`checkEventBinding`, also SURVIVED ×2 but is equivalent: the landed\n208|`AdmitProbe` refuses the same member with\n209|`terminal_backend_implementation_drift`, `TestRV2W_ManifestImplDriftCaughtByLandedAdmission`\n210|PASS under the plant ×2 — note only.)\n211|\n212|### P3-4 — Traceability and prose accuracy\n213|\n214|- (a) Row 57 and the registry's 5.2#18 discharge rest on a payload-member\n215|  census; no v1-v3-only reader exists on trunk, so \"a v1 reader stays\n216|  inert\" cannot be driven here. Restate as a bound (the v4-aware landed\n217|  reader retains v4 bytes verbatim and the query read writes nothing —\n218|  that half is driven by row 56).\n219|- (b) The 7.A#1 clause and the section 7.A binding cite\n220|  `terminal-instance-identity-exact` for \"the eight-form identity pin\n221|  through the same entry\", but that acceptance case lists no test that\n222|  reaches `AdmitProviderDescriptor` (`TestAdmitDescriptorRefusesForbiddenIdentity`\n223|  is cited nowhere in the registry). The clause is discharged by the landed\n224|  `terminal-provider-descriptor-7a` alone; add the descriptor test to the\n225|  case or drop the citation.\n226|- (c) `resolve.go` says \"Every failure refuses\n227|  terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch\" while the three shape pre-check\n228|  arms return uncoded `fmt.Errorf` values (`want 1..256`, `not sorted\n229|  unique`, `not a digest`); the pre-check itself is a third copy of a rule\n230|  the landed `canonicaljson` (and `axpane.checkEvidenceIDs`) already\n231|  enforce — defence in depth, but say so instead of \"every failure\".\n232|- (d) README: \"with the pinned protocol class on … the bootstrap binding\"\n233|  (see P3-1).\n234|\n235|### P3-5 — Deferral hygiene\n236|\n237|Restore and terminate-stale execution is deferred by kkh1an to \"the\n238|story's final leaf\" (`terminstance/doc.go`, rev3 P3-5 exit route) and by\n239|this leaf back to \"owner: terminstance\"; neither brief assigned it, so the\n240|Story closes with a normative operation pair that has no follow-up owner.\n241|Record the real owner (a Story follow-up task) in the results and LOGBOOK,\n242|and state in the results that the kkh1an `HandoffFailed` note is not\n243|applicable because this leaf wires no reporter.\n244|\n245|## 4. Reviewer instruments\n246|\n247|`probes/zz_review2_probe_test.go` (15 top-level probes: 4 CHARACTERIZATION\n248|failures = P2-1 (8 failing subtests), 3 witnesses `TestRV2W_*` and 8\n249|composition/agreement/bound probes PASS; two passes identical,\n250|`logs/12-probes-all-pass{1,2}.log`);\n251|`probes/zz_review2_digest_probe_test.go` (`logs/25`);\n252|`probes/review2_mutants.py` (9 narrowings + 2 controls against the whole\n253|committed termbind suite, two passes with identical verdicts, raw per-plant\n254|logs with exits and diffs in `logs/rv2-mutants-pass{1,2}/`: KILLED — M4\n255|native_reference 513, M7, M8, M10 attach foreign-session lookup, M11\n256|first-pair inversion, control K; SURVIVED — M3 equivalent-by-absence (P2-1),\n257|M5 non-equivalent (P2-1), M6 equivalent (landed admission), M9\n258|non-equivalent (P3-3), control C); `probes/run_witness_under_mutant.py` +\n259|`probes/run_witnesses.sh` (`logs/53`, `logs/rv2-witness-pass{1,2}/`);\n260|shipped harness reruns (`logs/harness/`); `logs/00`–`83`, coverprofile,\n261|tree listings, `REVIEW-MANIFEST.txt` (sha256 of every file).\n262|\n263|## 5. DoD walk (live merged checklist)\n264|\n265|Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable — yes for events,\n266|recovery and identity; the Binding parser under-enforces its table (P2-1).\n267|Positive/negative/compatibility/recovery tests pass with logs — yes.\n268|README/traceability without unsupported claims — mostly; P3-1/P3-4 name\n269|the sentences that outrun the tests. Uncommitted in the Story worktree —\n270|yes (tree OID equal, HEAD = checkpoint). Ratio — 59 of 60 measured against\n271|the claimed 60 of 60. Negative tests that fail when the gate admits — yes\n272|for the gates the rows name; two arms of the Binding parser have no gate\n273|to test. Narrowing mutant per gate — shipped 30/56/122 KILLED ×2 with\n274|working controls; my 9 narrowings: 5 KILLED ×2, 2 non-equivalent survivors\n275|with witnesses, 1 equivalent, 1 equivalent-by-absence. No source-text gate\n276|exists. Lint/build — clean. Outcome artefacts — attached, hygienic.\n277|Logbook — newest-first, additive, one factual error (P3-1). Implementation\n278|matches AC — not for the Binding table (P2-1). Fits the architecture — the\n279|identity rule is forked from the landed owner (P2-1); everything else\n280|composes. Tests green — yes. Gates attacked, not read — yes.\n281|\n282|## Rework scope (for the producer)\n283|\n284|1. `ParseTerminalBinding`: enforce `protocol_version` major 1 and\n285|   `extensions == {}` per §4.B; make `bindingIdentity` refuse JSON numbers\n286|   (at any depth) and nested duplicate members before the JCS transform,\n287|   preferably by reusing the landed `terminalbackend` rule; drive every\n288|   member arm of the Binding table negatively through the entry and ship\n289|   narrowing rows for the new arms plus `supersedes_binding_id`; re-run the\n290|   landed-agreement test with a numeric extension value.\n291|2. Commit `TestRV2W_RecoverGenerationBoundBeforeStatusRead` (or an\n292|   equivalent) with a harness row.\n293|3. `EmitResumed`: compose `sessprofile.CheckResumedPair` and a\n294|   known-checkpoint check, or state the bound explicitly.\n295|4. Correct the prose: harness notes for the two pre-scan rows and LOGBOOK\n296|   F2 (append a correction), README's \"pinned protocol class … bootstrap\n297|   binding\", `resolve.go`'s \"every failure\", row 57 / 5.2#18 as a bound,\n298|   the 7.A citation.\n299|5. Record the restore/terminate-stale follow-up owner and the\n300|   `HandoffFailed` non-applicability in the results and LOGBOOK.\n301|6. Rerun your own package suite, the three harnesses and the configured\n302|   suite before handoff; keep the candidate uncommitted on the Story\n303|   branch.\n304|\n305|Verdict recorded by RUN-260918-acd5a8 by routing `to-dev`; no product edits,\n306|commits, checkpoints or integration were performed; the isolated copies are\n307|deleted after attachment. `commit_ack` is not supplied.","final_result":true}}}
