{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c935","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3fc-2962-7bc0-91c2-787ae4899fa1"},"sequence":757,"recorded_at":1780531400001509,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b3fe-b9ab-7941-8fbd-a5c7c29d5864"},"task_id":"01a0b3fe-b9ab-7941-8fbd-a5c7c29d5864","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b3fe-b9ab-7941-8fbd-a5c7c29d5864","chunk":"Read text file `internal/termbind/mutant_harness.py`.\n1|#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2|\"\"\"Narrowing-mutant harness for internal/termbind.\n3|\n4|Every gate ships a narrowing mutant: the gate stays present and is\n5|weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and\n6|the named killer tests must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that\n7|the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence; row D-emit-noresolve is\n8|the one explicitly supplementary arm-delete (the producer-named drop),\n9|labeled as such and not counted as any gate's narrowing.\n10|\n11|Each row runs M (mutate production files in place), R (run the scoped Go\n12|killers through the production entries), V (verdict from the Go exit code\n13|plus a FAIL kill-line: KILLED iff R fails with a test failure line,\n14|SURVIVED iff R passes, ERROR for anything else -- unapplied patches,\n15|build breaks, timeouts). M failures and R infrastructure errors are\n16|ERROR, never kills or survivals. Files are restored from backups after\n17|every row, pass or fail.\n18|\n19|Row C-control is the harmless control: a comment-only edit that must\n20|SURVIVE, proving the harness observes test outcomes instead of\n21|hard-coding kills.\n22|\n23|Two plants are honestly not rows: attach cannot emit an event because\n24|Attach takes no repository (absence by construction, proven by\n25|TestAttachEmitsNeitherEventNorStateChange -- no text plant can add a\n26|write), and the lease-authority narrowing belongs to the adopted axpane\n27|rows N-emit-mutation and N-emit-losing-epoch (composition pinned here by\n28|TestEmitUnderLosingLeaseRefuses).\n29|\n30|Usage:\n31|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/termbind/mutant_harness.py\n32|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/termbind/mutant_harness.py N-identity-pid\n33|  AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE=1 PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/termbind/mutant_harness.py N-identity-pid\n34|\"\"\"\n35|\n36|import os\n37|import shutil\n38|import subprocess\n39|import sys\n40|import tempfile\n41|from dataclasses import dataclass\n42|from pathlib import Path\n43|\n44|REPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n45|PACKAGE = \"internal/termbind\"\n46|\n47|DD_DIGEST = \"sha256:\" + \"dd\" * 32\n48|OTHER_OP = \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ac\"\n49|\n50|\n51|@dataclass(frozen=True)\n52|class Mutant:\n53|    name: str\n54|    path: str\n55|    find: str\n56|    replace: str\n57|    count: int\n58|    run: str\n59|    expect: str\n60|    note: str\n61|    find2: str = \"\"\n62|    replace2: str = \"\"\n63|    count2: int = 0\n64|\n65|\n66|IDENTITY_KILLERS = (\n67|    \"(TestCheckInstanceIdentityRefusesForbiddenForms\"\n68|    \"|TestParseTerminalBindingRefusesForbiddenIdentity\"\n69|    \"|TestAdmitMutationContextRefusesForbiddenIdentity\"\n70|    \"|TestAdmitStatusBodyRefusesForbiddenIdentity\"\n71|    \"|TestAttachRefusesForbiddenIdentity)\"\n72|)\n73|\n74|MUTANTS = [\n75|    Mutant(\n76|        name=\"N-identity-pid\",\n77|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/identity.go\",\n78|        find='\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(value); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn &terminalbackend.Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"terminal instance identity\"}\\n\\t}\\n',\n79|        replace='\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(value); err != nil && value != \"12345\" {\\n\\t\\treturn &terminalbackend.Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"terminal instance identity\"}\\n\\t}\\n',\n80|        count=1,\n81|        run=IDENTITY_KILLERS,\n82|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n83|        note=\"Admits exactly the PID form at the shared identity gate; every other forbidden form still refuses on all five surfaces.\",\n84|    ),\n85|    Mutant(\n86|        name=\"N-identity-endpoint\",\n87|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/identity.go\",\n88|        find='\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(value); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn &terminalbackend.Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"terminal instance identity\"}\\n\\t}\\n',\n89|        replace='\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(value); err != nil && value != \"10.0.0.9:2222\" {\\n\\t\\treturn &terminalbackend.Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"terminal instance identity\"}\\n\\t}\\n',\n90|        count=1,\n91|        run=IDENTITY_KILLERS,\n92|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n93|        note=\"Admits exactly the endpoint form at the shared identity gate; every other forbidden form still refuses on all five surfaces.\",\n94|    ),\n95|    Mutant(\n96|        name=\"N-binding-members\",\n97|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/identity.go\",\n98|        find=\"\\tif len(members) != len(bindingMembers) {\\n\",\n99|        replace=\"\\tif len(members) != len(bindingMembers) && len(members) != len(bindingMembers)+1 {\\n\",\n100|        count=1,\n101|        run=\"TestParseTerminalBindingClosedShape/extra_member\",\n102|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n103|        note=\"Admits exactly one extra binding member; missing members and two extras still refuse.\",\n104|    ),\n105|    Mutant(\n106|        name=\"N-binding-identity\",\n107|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/identity.go\",\n108|        find=\"\\tif recomputed != bindingID {\\n\",\n109|        replace=f'\\tif recomputed != bindingID && bindingID != \"{DD_DIGEST}\" {{\\n',\n110|        count=1,\n111|        run=\"TestParseTerminalBindingClosedShape/wrong_self_id\",\n112|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n113|        note=\"Admits exactly the wrong self-ID fixture; other identity breaks still refuse.\",\n114|    ),\n115|    Mutant(\n116|        name=\"N-binding-generation\",\n117|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/identity.go\",\n118|        find=\"\\tif _, err := terminalbackend.GenerationDigest(generation); err != nil {\\n\",\n119|        replace=\"\\tif _, err := terminalbackend.GenerationDigest(generation); err != nil && len(generation) != 257 {\\n\",\n120|        count=1,\n121|        run=\"TestParseTerminalBindingClosedShape/generation_bounds\",\n122|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n123|        note=\"Admits exactly the 257-character generation; length 0 and 258+ still refuse.\",\n124|    ),\n125|    Mutant(\n126|        name=\"N-prescan-context\",\n127|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/identity.go\",\n128|        find=\"\\treturn CheckInstanceIdentity(value)\\n\",\n129|        replace='\\tif value == \"12345\" {\\n\\t\\treturn nil\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn CheckInstanceIdentity(value)\\n',\n130|        count=1,\n131|        run=\"TestAdmitMutationContextRefusesForbiddenIdentity/pid\",\n132|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n133|        note=\"Skips the context pre-scan exactly for the PID form; the landed plain refusal surfaces instead of the pinned code.\",\n134|    ),\n135|    Mutant(\n136|        name=\"N-status-prescan\",\n137|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/identity.go\",\n138|        find=\"\\tif err := CheckInstanceIdentity(value); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn terminstance.StatusBody{}, err\\n\\t}\\n\",\n139|        replace='\\tif err := CheckInstanceIdentity(value); err != nil && value != \"12345\" {\\n\\t\\treturn terminstance.StatusBody{}, err\\n\\t}\\n',\n140|        count=1,\n141|        run=\"TestAdmitStatusBodyRefusesForbiddenIdentity/pid\",\n142|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n143|        note=\"Skips the status pre-scan exactly for the PID form; the landed plain refusal surfaces instead of the pinned code.\",\n144|    ),\n145|    Mutant(\n146|        name=\"N-evidence-257\",\n147|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/resolve.go\",\n148|        find=\"\\tif len(ids) < minEvidenceIDs || len(ids) > maxEvidenceIDs {\\n\",\n149|        replace=\"\\tif len(ids) < minEvidenceIDs || len(ids) > maxEvidenceIDs+1 {\\n\",\n150|        count=1,\n151|        run=\"TestResolveEvidenceShapeBounds/257_refuses\",\n152|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n153|        note=\"Admits exactly 257 evidence IDs past the shape arm; 258 still refuses.\",\n154|    ),\n155|    Mutant(\n156|        name=\"N-evidence-0\",\n157|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/resolve.go\",\n158|        find=\"\\tif len(ids) < minEvidenceIDs || len(ids) > maxEvidenceIDs {\\n\",\n159|        replace=\"\\tif len(ids) < minEvidenceIDs-1 || len(ids) > maxEvidenceIDs {\\n\",\n160|        count=1,\n161|        run=\"TestResolveEvidenceShapeBounds/empty_refuses\",\n162|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n163|        note=\"Admits exactly the empty evidence set past the shape arm; the partition refusal surfaces instead of the bound.\",\n164|    ),\n165|    Mutant(\n166|        name=\"N-evidence-dup\",\n167|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/resolve.go\",\n168|        find=\"\\t\\tif index > 0 && id <= previous {\\n\",\n169|        replace=\"\\t\\tif index > 0 && id < previous {\\n\",\n170|        count=1,\n171|        run=\"TestResolveEvidenceShapeBounds/duplicate_refuses\",\n172|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n173|        note=\"Admits exactly duplicate evidence IDs; inversions still refuse.\",\n174|    ),\n175|    Mutant(\n176|        name=\"N-evidence-unsorted\",\n177|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/resolve.go\",\n178|        find=\"\\t\\tif index > 0 && id <= previous {\\n\",\n179|        replace=\"\\t\\tif index > 1 && id <= previous {\\n\",\n180|        count=1,\n181|        run=\"TestResolveEvidenceShapeBounds/unsorted_refuses\",\n182|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n183|        note=\"Skips exactly the first-pair order comparison; later inversions still refuse.\",\n184|    ),\n185|    Mutant(\n186|        name=\"N-resolve-kind\",\n187|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/resolve.go\",\n188|        find='\\tdefault:\\n\\t\\treturn \"\", mismatchRefusal(\"evidence kind\")\\n',\n189|        replace='\\tdefault:\\n\\t\\tif schema == \"ax-terminal-endpoint\" {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn terminalbackend.SchemaCapabilityEvidence, nil\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\treturn \"\", mismatchRefusal(\"evidence kind\")\\n',\n190|        count=1,\n191|        run=\"(TestResolveEvidenceRefusesForeignKinds|TestEmitResolvesEvidence)/(endpoint|foreign_kind)\",\n192|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n193|        note=\"Admits exactly the endpoint document as evidence; every other foreign kind still refuses, at the direct and emission entries.\",\n194|    ),\n195|    Mutant(\n196|        name=\"N-resolve-manifest-count\",\n197|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/resolve.go\",\n198|        find='\\t\\tcase terminalbackend.SchemaManifest:\\n\\t\\t\\tif manifestFound {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\treturn empty, mismatchRefusal(\"evidence manifest\")\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n',\n199|        replace='\\t\\tcase terminalbackend.SchemaManifest:\\n\\t\\t\\tif manifestFound && len(ids) < 4 {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\treturn empty, mismatchRefusal(\"evidence manifest\")\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n',\n200|        count=1,\n201|        run=\"TestResolveEvidenceRequiresManifestAndProbe/second_manifest\",\n202|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n203|        note=\"Admits exactly the four-ID double-manifest set; other ambiguous sets still refuse.\",\n204|    ),\n205|    Mutant(\n206|        name=\"N-resolve-binding\",\n207|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/resolve.go\",\n208|        find=\"\\t\\tif object.TerminalBackendID != tuple.BackendID || object.ImplementationVersion != tuple.ImplementationVersion || object.ProtocolVersion != tuple.ProtocolVersion {\\n\",\n209|        replace=\"\\t\\tif object.TerminalBackendID != tuple.BackendID || object.ImplementationVersion != tuple.ImplementationVersion {\\n\",\n210|        count=1,\n211|        run=\"TestResolveEvidenceBindsEventTuple/protocol_drift_evidence\",\n212|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n213|        note=\"Drops exactly the evidence protocol arm; backend and implementation drift still refuse at this gate.\",\n214|    ),\n215|    Mutant(\n216|        name=\"N-resolve-identity\",\n217|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/resolve.go\",\n218|        find=\"\\tif !named[manifest.ManifestID] || !named[probe.ProbeID] {\\n\",\n219|        replace=\"\\tif !named[manifest.ManifestID] {\\n\",\n220|        count=1,\n221|        run=\"TestResolveEvidenceRejectsSubstitution/probe_alias\",\n222|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n223|        note=\"Drops exactly the probe half of the substitution check; manifest and evidence aliases still refuse.\",\n224|    ),\n225|    Mutant(\n226|        name=\"N-resolve-admission\",\n227|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/resolve.go\",\n228|        find=\"\\tadmitted, err := registry.AdmitProbe(manifestRaw, probeRaw, evidenceRaws, rawGeneration, now, verify)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn empty, err\\n\\t}\\n\",\n229|        replace=\"\\tadmitted, err := registry.AdmitProbe(manifestRaw, probeRaw, evidenceRaws, rawGeneration, now, verify)\\n\\tif err != nil && !terminalbackend.IsDrift(err) {\\n\\t\\treturn empty, err\\n\\t}\\n\",\n230|        count=1,\n231|        run=\"TestResolveEvidenceDrivesLandedAdmission/registry_drift\",\n232|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n233|        note=\"Swallows exactly the landed drift refusal; every other admission refusal still surfaces.\",\n234|    ),\n235|    Mutant(\n236|        name=\"N-emit-created-v3\",\n237|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/emit.go\",\n238|        find=\"\\tparams.EventType = eventTerminalCreated\\n\\tparams.SchemaVersion = eventSchemaV4\\n\",\n239|        replace='\\tparams.EventType = eventTerminalCreated\\n\\tparams.SchemaVersion = \"3.0.0\"\\n',\n240|        count=1,\n241|        run=\"TestEmitTerminalCreatedRoundTrip\",\n242|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n243|        note=\"Emits the created payload at v3; the canonical owner refuses the v4 members under the v3 shape.\",\n244|    ),\n245|    Mutant(\n246|        name=\"N-emit-resumed-v3\",\n247|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/emit.go\",\n248|        find=\"\\tparams.EventType = eventSessionResumed\\n\\tparams.SchemaVersion = eventSchemaV4\\n\",\n249|        replace='\\tparams.EventType = eventSessionResumed\\n\\tparams.SchemaVersion = \"3.0.0\"\\n',\n250|        count=1,\n251|        run=\"TestEmitResumedRoundTrip\",\n252|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n253|        note=\"Emits the resumed payload at v3; the canonical owner refuses the v4 members under the v3 shape.\",\n254|    ),\n255|    Mutant(\n256|        name=\"D-emit-noresolve\",\n257|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/emit.go\",\n258|        find=\"\\tresolved, err := ResolveEvidence(facts.EvidenceIDs, tupleFromFacts(facts), admission.Registry, admission.Universe, admission.RawGeneration, admission.Now, admission.Verify)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn empty, nil, ResolvedEvidence{}, err\\n\\t}\\n\",\n259|        replace=\"\\tresolved := ResolvedEvidence{}\\n\",\n260|        count=2,\n261|        run=\"TestEmitResolvesEvidence\",\n262|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n263|        note=\"ARM-DELETE, supplementary: drops resolution at both emission entries; unresolvable evidence proceeds to append. Not counted as any gate's narrowing.\",\n264|    ),\n265|    Mutant(\n266|        name=\"N-recover-mismatch\",\n267|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/recover.go\",\n268|        find=\"\\t\\tif anchored && anchor.OperationID != request.BootstrapOperationID && request.WindowOpen {\\n\",\n269|        replace=f'\\t\\tif anchored && anchor.OperationID != request.BootstrapOperationID && request.WindowOpen && request.BootstrapOperationID != \"{OTHER_OP}\" {{\\n',\n270|        count=1,\n271|        run=\"TestRecoverCreateChangedOperationInWindowRefuses\",\n272|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n273|        note=\"Admits exactly the fixture changed operation in-window; other changed operations still refuse.\",\n274|    ),\n275|    Mutant(\n276|        name=\"N-recover-second-child\",\n277|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/recover.go\",\n278|        find=\"\\tif !found {\\n\\t\\tif report.IdentityMatch && report.State == terminalbackend.StateAbsent {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn RecoveryVerdict{Outcome: RecoveryAbsent, State: report.State, Retry: terminstance.DispositionReplaySame}, nil\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\treturn RecoveryVerdict{Outcome: RecoveryUnavailable, State: report.State, Retry: terminstance.DispositionStatusFirst}, nil\\n\\t}\\n\",\n279|        replace=\"\\tif !found {\\n\\t\\tif report.IdentityMatch && report.State == terminalbackend.StateAbsent {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn RecoveryVerdict{Outcome: RecoveryAbsent, State: report.State, Retry: terminstance.DispositionReplaySame}, nil\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\treturn RecoveryVerdict{Outcome: RecoveryChild, State: report.State, Retry: terminstance.DispositionReplaySame}, nil\\n\\t}\\n\",\n280|        count=1,\n281|        run=\"TestRecoverCreateNeverClaimsAbsent/unbound_live_instance\",\n282|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n283|        note=\"Adopts exactly the unbound live instance as a second child; proven absence still vacates.\",\n284|    ),\n285|    Mutant(\n286|        name=\"N-recover-contradiction-absent\",\n287|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/recover.go\",\n288|        find=\"\\tif !report.IdentityMatch {\\n\\t\\treturn RecoveryVerdict{Outcome: RecoveryUnavailable, State: report.State, Retry: terminstance.DispositionStatusFirst}, nil\\n\\t}\\n\",\n289|        replace=\"\\tif !report.IdentityMatch {\\n\\t\\treturn RecoveryVerdict{Outcome: RecoveryAbsent, State: report.State, Retry: terminstance.DispositionReplaySame}, nil\\n\\t}\\n\",\n290|        count=1,\n291|        run=\"TestRecoverCreateNeverClaimsAbsent/bound_contradiction\",\n292|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n293|        note=\"Claims exactly the bound contradiction as absence; matched observations keep their verdicts.\",\n294|    ),\n295|    Mutant(\n296|        name=\"N-recover-creating-child\",\n297|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/recover.go\",\n298|        find=\"\\tcase terminalbackend.StateCreating, terminalbackend.StateUnavailable:\\n\",\n299|        replace=\"\\tcase terminalbackend.StateUnavailable:\\n\",\n300|        count=1,\n301|        run=\"TestRecoverCreateNeverClaimsAbsent/creating_interim\",\n302|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n303|        note=\"Admits exactly the creating interim as a child; backend-reported unavailable still parks.\",\n304|    ),\n305|    Mutant(\n306|        name=\"N-recover-status-error\",\n307|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/recover.go\",\n308|        find='\\treport, err := deps.Engine.ExecuteStatus(ctx, body, \"\", deps.Admitted)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn empty, err\\n\\t}\\n',\n309|        replace='\\treport, err := deps.Engine.ExecuteStatus(ctx, body, \"\", deps.Admitted)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn RecoveryVerdict{Outcome: RecoveryAbsent, State: terminalbackend.StateAbsent, Retry: terminstance.DispositionReplaySame}, nil\\n\\t}\\n',\n310|        count=1,\n311|        run=\"TestRecoverCreateUnknownIsNotAbsent/status_read_failure\",\n312|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n313|        note=\"Launders exactly the status read failure as proven absence; reported observations keep their verdicts.\",\n314|    ),\n315|    Mutant(\n316|        name=\"N-recover-window\",\n317|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/recover.go\",\n318|        find=\"\\t\\tif anchored && anchor.OperationID != request.BootstrapOperationID && request.WindowOpen {\\n\",\n319|        replace=\"\\t\\tif anchored && anchor.OperationID != request.BootstrapOperationID && !request.WindowOpen {\\n\",\n320|        count=1,\n321|        run=\"TestRecoverCreateChangedOperationInWindowRefuses\",\n322|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n323|        note=\"Inverts exactly the window bit; post-window changed pairs refuse while in-window proceeds.\",\n324|    ),\n325|    Mutant(\n326|        name=\"N-attach-conflict\",\n327|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/attach.go\",\n328|        find=\"\\t\\tif stored.Transport != transport || stored.InputAuthorized != inputAuthorized {\\n\",\n329|        replace=\"\\t\\tif stored.Transport != transport {\\n\",\n330|        count=1,\n331|        run=\"TestAttachConflictRefusesMismatch\",\n332|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n333|        note=\"Drops exactly the input half of the conflict conjunction at both the pre-check and the commit-converge comparison; transport conflicts still refuse.\",\n334|        find2=\"\\t\\t\\tif winner.Transport != transport || winner.InputAuthorized != inputAuthorized {\\n\",\n335|        replace2=\"\\t\\t\\tif winner.Transport != transport {\\n\",\n336|        count2=1,\n337|    ),\n338|    Mutant(\n339|        name=\"N-attach-transport\",\n340|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/attach.go\",\n341|        find=\"\\tif !isAttachTransport(transport) {\\n\",\n342|        replace='\\tif !isAttachTransport(transport) && transport != \"smoke_signal\" {\\n',\n343|        count=1,\n344|        run=\"TestAttachTransportVocabulary/unknown_transport\",\n345|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n346|        note=\"Admits exactly the smoke_signal transport past the enum; the landed vocabulary refusal surfaces instead of this gate's.\",\n347|    ),\n348|    Mutant(\n349|        name=\"N-attach-auth-replay\",\n350|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/attach.go\",\n351|        find=\"\\tauth, err := terminalbackend.ParseAttachAuthorization(authRaw)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn empty, false, err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif err := terminalbackend.CheckAttachRequest(auth, transport, inputAuthorized, now); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn empty, false, err\\n\\t}\\n\\tstored, found, err := store.Lookup(sessionID, instanceID, clientID)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn empty, false, err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif found {\\n\",\n352|        replace=\"\\tstored, found, err := store.Lookup(sessionID, instanceID, clientID)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn empty, false, err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif found {\\n\\t\\treturn stored, true, nil\\n\\t}\\n\\tauth, err := terminalbackend.ParseAttachAuthorization(authRaw)\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn empty, false, err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif err := terminalbackend.CheckAttachRequest(auth, transport, inputAuthorized, now); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn empty, false, err\\n\\t}\\n\\tif false {\\n\",\n353|        count=1,\n354|        run=\"TestAttachRequiresLiveAuth/replay_with_expired_auth\",\n355|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n356|        note=\"Skips authorization exactly on the replay path; fresh attaches still authorize.\",\n357|    ),\n358|    Mutant(\n359|        name=\"N-attach-key\",\n360|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/attach.go\",\n361|        find='\\treturn filepath.Join(store.instanceDir(instanceID), clientID+\".json\")\\n',\n362|        replace='\\treturn filepath.Join(store.instanceDir(instanceID), \"client.json\")\\n',\n363|        count=1,\n364|        run=\"TestAttachSecondClientRecordsAlongside\",\n365|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n366|        note=\"Collapses exactly the client axis of the idempotency key; the instance axis still separates.\",\n367|    ),\n368|    Mutant(\n369|        name=\"C-control\",\n370|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/doc.go\",\n371|        find=\"// Division of authority (composed, never forked): v4 payload construction\\n\",\n372|        replace=\"// Division of authority (composed, never forked; control): v4 payload construction\\n\",\n373|        count=1,\n374|        run=\"TestCheckInstanceIdentityAdmitsUUIDv7\",\n375|        expect=\"SURVIVED\",\n376|        note=\"Harmless control: a comment-only edit must survive.\",\n377|    ),\n378|]\n379|\n380|\n381|def apply(mutant: Mutant, original: str) -> str:\n382|    patched = original.replace(mutant.find, mutant.replace)\n383|    if mutant.find2:\n384|        patched = patched.replace(mutant.find2, mutant.replace2)\n385|    return patched\n386|\n387|\n388|def run_mutant(mutant: Mutant) -> str:\n389|    target = REPO / mutant.path\n390|    original = target.read_text()\n391|    found = original.count(mutant.find)\n392|    if found != mutant.count:\n393|        return f\"ERROR: {mutant.name}: patch anchors {found}, want {mutant.count}\"\n394|    if mutant.find2:\n395|        found2 = original.count(mutant.find2)\n396|        if found2 != mutant.count2:\n397|            return f\"ERROR: {mutant.name}: second anchors {found2}, want {mutant.count2}\"\n398|    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as staging:\n399|        backup = Path(staging) / \"backup\"\n400|        shutil.copy2(target, backup)\n401|        try:\n402|            target.write_text(apply(mutant, original))\n403|            run = subprocess.run(\n404|                [\"go\", \"test\", f\"./{PACKAGE}/\", \"-run\", mutant.run, \"-count=1\"],\n405|                cwd=REPO,\n406|                capture_output=True,\n407|                text=True,\n408|                timeout=300,\n409|            )\n410|        finally:\n411|            shutil.copy2(backup, target)\n412|    output = (run.stdout + run.stderr).strip()\n413|    if os.environ.get(\"AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE\") == \"1\":\n414|        print(f\"--- raw: {mutant.name}: exit {run.returncode} ---\", flush=True)\n415|        print(output, flush=True)\n416|        print(f\"--- end raw: {mutant.name} ---\", flush=True)\n417|    if 'build failed' in output or '\\n# ' in output or output.startswith('# '):\n418|        return f\"ERROR: {mutant.name}: build broke under the patch\"\n419|    if run.returncode == 0:\n420|        verdict = \"SURVIVED\"\n421|    elif '--- FAIL' in output or 'FAIL:' in output:\n422|        verdict = \"KILLED\"\n423|    else:\n424|        return f\"ERROR: {mutant.name}: exit {run.returncode} with no kill line\"\n425|    mark = \"ok\" if verdict == mutant.expect else \"MISMATCH\"\n426|    return f\"{mark}: {mutant.name}: {verdict} (want {mutant.expect}) :: {mutant.note} [exit {run.returncode}]\"\n427|\n428|\n429|def main(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n430|    selected = [m for m in MUTANTS if not argv or m.name in argv]\n431|    if argv and len(selected) != len(argv):\n432|        unknown = sorted(set(argv) - {m.name for m in selected})\n433|        print(f\"unknown mutants: {', '.join(unknown)}\")\n434|        return 2\n435|    failures = 0\n436|    for mutant in selected:\n437|        try:\n438|            line = run_mutant(mutant)\n439|        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n440|            line = f\"ERROR: {mutant.name}: killer timed out\"\n441|        print(line, flush=True)\n442|        if not line.startswith(\"ok:\"):\n443|            failures += 1\n444|    return 1 if failures else 0\n445|\n446|\n447|if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n448|    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c937","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3fc-2962-7bc0-91c2-787ae4899fa1"},"sequence":758,"recorded_at":1780531400001511,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b3fe-b9ab-7941-8fbd-a5c7c29d5864"},"task_id":"01a0b3fe-b9ab-7941-8fbd-a5c7c29d5864","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0b3fe-b9ab-7941-8fbd-a5c7c29d5864"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c939","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3fc-2962-7bc0-91c2-787ae4899fa1"},"sequence":759,"recorded_at":1780531400001513,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a"},"call_id":"call_01a0b3feb69f7646942fecaaa57ed217","text":"Read text file `internal/termbind/mutant_harness.py`.\n1|#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2|\"\"\"Narrowing-mutant harness for internal/termbind.\n3|\n4|Every gate ships a narrowing mutant: the gate stays present and is\n5|weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and\n6|the named killer tests must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that\n7|the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence; row D-emit-noresolve is\n8|the one explicitly supplementary arm-delete (the producer-named drop),\n9|labeled as such and not counted as any gate's narrowing.\n10|\n11|Each row runs M (mutate production files in place), R (run the scoped Go\n12|killers through the production entries), V (verdict from the Go exit code\n13|plus a FAIL kill-line: KILLED iff R fails with a test failure line,\n14|SURVIVED iff R passes, ERROR for anything else -- unapplied patches,\n15|build breaks, timeouts). M failures and R infrastructure errors are\n16|ERROR, never kills or survivals. Files are restored from backups after\n17|every row, pass or fail.\n18|\n19|Row C-control is the harmless control: a comment-only edit that must\n20|SURVIVE, proving the harness observes test outcomes instead of\n21|hard-coding kills.\n22|\n23|Two plants are honestly not rows: attach cannot emit an event because\n24|Attach takes no repository (absence by construction, proven by\n25|TestAttachEmitsNeitherEventNorStateChange -- no text plant can add a\n26|write), and the lease-authority narrowing belongs to the adopted axpane\n27|rows N-emit-mutation and N-emit-losing-epoch (composition pinned here by\n28|TestEmitUnderLosingLeaseRefuses).\n29|\n30|Usage:\n31|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/termbind/mutant_harness.py\n32|  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/termbind/mutant_harness.py N-identity-pid\n33|  AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE=1 PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/termbind/mutant_harness.py N-identity-pid\n34|\"\"\"\n35|\n36|import os\n37|import shutil\n38|import subprocess\n39|import sys\n40|import tempfile\n41|from dataclasses import dataclass\n42|from pathlib import Path\n43|\n44|REPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n45|PACKAGE = \"internal/termbind\"\n46|\n47|DD_DIGEST = \"sha256:\" + \"dd\" * 32\n48|OTHER_OP = \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ac\"\n49|\n50|\n51|@dataclass(frozen=True)\n52|class Mutant:\n53|    name: str\n54|    path: str\n55|    find: str\n56|    replace: str\n57|    count: int\n58|    run: str\n59|    expect: str\n60|    note: str\n61|    find2: str = \"\"\n62|    replace2: str = \"\"\n63|    count2: int = 0\n64|\n65|\n66|IDENTITY_KILLERS = (\n67|    \"(TestCheckInstanceIdentityRefusesForbiddenForms\"\n68|    \"|TestParseTerminalBindingRefusesForbiddenIdentity\"\n69|    \"|TestAdmitMutationContextRefusesForbiddenIdentity\"\n70|    \"|TestAdmitStatusBodyRefusesForbiddenIdentity\"\n71|    \"|TestAttachRefusesForbiddenIdentity)\"\n72|)\n73|\n74|MUTANTS = [\n75|    Mutant(\n76|        name=\"N-identity-pid\",\n77|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/identity.go\",\n78|        find='\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(value); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn &terminalbackend.Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"terminal instance identity\"}\\n\\t}\\n',\n79|        replace='\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(value); err != nil && value != \"12345\" {\\n\\t\\treturn &terminalbackend.Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"terminal instance identity\"}\\n\\t}\\n',\n80|        count=1,\n81|        run=IDENTITY_KILLERS,\n82|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n83|        note=\"Admits exactly the PID form at the shared identity gate; every other forbidden form still refuses on all five surfaces.\",\n84|    ),\n85|    Mutant(\n86|        name=\"N-identity-endpoint\",\n87|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/identity.go\",\n88|        find='\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(value); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn &terminalbackend.Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"terminal instance identity\"}\\n\\t}\\n',\n89|        replace='\\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(value); err != nil && value != \"10.0.0.9:2222\" {\\n\\t\\treturn &terminalbackend.Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"terminal instance identity\"}\\n\\t}\\n',\n90|        count=1,\n91|        run=IDENTITY_KILLERS,\n92|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n93|        note=\"Admits exactly the endpoint form at the shared identity gate; every other forbidden form still refuses on all five surfaces.\",\n94|    ),\n95|    Mutant(\n96|        name=\"N-binding-members\",\n97|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/identity.go\",\n98|        find=\"\\tif len(members) != len(bindingMembers) {\\n\",\n99|        replace=\"\\tif len(members) != len(bindingMembers) && len(members) != len(bindingMembers)+1 {\\n\",\n100|        count=1,\n101|        run=\"TestParseTerminalBindingClosedShape/extra_member\",\n102|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n103|        note=\"Admits exactly one extra binding member; missing members and two extras still refuse.\",\n104|    ),\n105|    Mutant(\n106|        name=\"N-binding-identity\",\n107|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/identity.go\",\n108|        find=\"\\tif recomputed != bindingID {\\n\",\n109|        replace=f'\\tif recomputed != bindingID && bindingID != \"{DD_DIGEST}\" {{\\n',\n110|        count=1,\n111|        run=\"TestParseTerminalBindingClosedShape/wrong_self_id\",\n112|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n113|        note=\"Admits exactly the wrong self-ID fixture; other identity breaks still refuse.\",\n114|    ),\n115|    Mutant(\n116|        name=\"N-binding-generation\",\n117|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/identity.go\",\n118|        find=\"\\tif _, err := terminalbackend.GenerationDigest(generation); err != nil {\\n\",\n119|        replace=\"\\tif _, err := terminalbackend.GenerationDigest(generation); err != nil && len(generation) != 257 {\\n\",\n120|        count=1,\n121|        run=\"TestParseTerminalBindingClosedShape/generation_bounds\",\n122|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n123|        note=\"Admits exactly the 257-character generation; length 0 and 258+ still refuse.\",\n124|    ),\n125|    Mutant(\n126|        name=\"N-prescan-context\",\n127|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/identity.go\",\n128|        find=\"\\treturn CheckInstanceIdentity(value)\\n\",\n129|        replace='\\tif value == \"12345\" {\\n\\t\\treturn nil\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn CheckInstanceIdentity(value)\\n',\n130|        count=1,\n131|        run=\"TestAdmitMutationContextRefusesForbiddenIdentity/pid\",\n132|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n133|        note=\"Skips the context pre-scan exactly for the PID form; the landed plain refusal surfaces instead of the pinned code.\",\n134|    ),\n135|    Mutant(\n136|        name=\"N-status-prescan\",\n137|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/identity.go\",\n138|        find=\"\\tif err := CheckInstanceIdentity(value); err != nil {\\n\\t\\treturn terminstance.StatusBody{}, err\\n\\t}\\n\",\n139|        replace='\\tif err := CheckInstanceIdentity(value); err != nil && value != \"12345\" {\\n\\t\\treturn terminstance.StatusBody{}, err\\n\\t}\\n',\n140|        count=1,\n141|        run=\"TestAdmitStatusBodyRefusesForbiddenIdentity/pid\",\n142|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n143|        note=\"Skips the status pre-scan exactly for the PID form; the landed plain refusal surfaces instead of the pinned code.\",\n144|    ),\n145|    Mutant(\n146|        name=\"N-evidence-257\",\n147|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/resolve.go\",\n148|        find=\"\\ti