{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cb3f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3fc-2962-7bc0-91c2-787ae4899fa1"},"sequence":1018,"recorded_at":1780531400002031,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a"},"call_id":"call_01a0b3ffee9f77ca9719ff4aeb876dcf","text":"Read text file `/tmp/tb2056/results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2056mm results — implement-terminal-binding-events-and-recovery\n2|\n3|Final leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe (ax-pane-and-terminal-instance-binding, EPIC M1).\n4|Candidate: UNCOMMITTED working tree on branch `task-board/story/STORY-260830-ptxkqe`\n5|atop checkpoint ca1c1d9 (predecessors 1geqhj + kkh1an signed checkpoints).\n6|No commit, rebase, or branch operation performed by this run.\n7|\n8|Trunk: origin/main == c3aae73 at handoff (verified `git fetch origin main`;\n9|merge-base == origin/main), so no `refresh-candidate` was needed.\n10|`task-board.config.json` is byte-identical to HEAD (verified\n11|`git diff HEAD --quiet -- task-board.config.json`). No validation command added.\n12|\n13|Normative source: SPEC.v0.7.0 (v0.7.0 adoption on trunk at spawn).\n14|Predecessor outcomes and the whole branch delta were read before starting;\n15|the corrected 1geqhj rev2 authoring path (no `session.parked` under an\n16|unheld lease, `fencing.AuthorizeMutation` composed) is built on, not forked.\n17|\n18|## Deliverable\n19|\n20|New `internal/termbind` composing the landed owners and the story's own\n21|`axpane`/`terminstance` (never forked):\n22|\n23|- (1) v4 payloads: `EmitTerminalCreated` / `EmitResumed` author the exact\n24|  `terminal.created` and `session.resumed` payloads through the landed\n25|  `sessrepo` append path under a locally held lease; v1-v3 registry untouched.\n26|- (2) Evidence resolution: `ResolveEvidence` resolves each event's\n27|  `evidence_ids` to exactly one Manifest, one Probe, and the Capability\n28|  Evidence objects bound to the event tuple through landed\n29|  `Registry.AdmitProbe`. Eleven foreign targets refuse (native reference,\n30|  generation string, socket, pipe, endpoint, token, credential, terminal\n31|  output, PID/handle, live-process fact, plus capability-echo); the binding\n32|  digest is opaque — no Binding object, native_reference, or generation\n33|  string is reachable through the event.\n34|- (3) Identity refusal: `CheckInstanceIdentity` + `ParseTerminalBinding` +\n35|  operation-body pre-scans refuse all eight forbidden forms\n36|  (PID, handle, socket, path, pipe, URL, token, endpoint) with the pinned\n37|  `terminal_backend_protocol_error` on the Binding, descriptor (adopted\n38|  landed entry), operation bodies, bootstrap binding, and attach receipts;\n39|  CLI Result 4 is a tripwire-pinned stated bound (unimplemented surface).\n40|- (4) Lost-result recovery: `RecoverCreate` is read-only — one status read\n41|  plus the durable (session_id, bootstrap_operation_id) binding proves\n42|  absence or identifies the ONE child; unprovable shapes yield `unavailable`\n43|  with `status_first`, never a second child, never a false absence claim.\n44|  Window derives from the fold newest (`sessstate.Reduce`), never from the\n45|  vacuous epoch-1 lease checkpoint field.\n46|- (5) Skew and authority: takeover selects an admitted backend with a NEW\n47|  digest and event (append-only, no fork); attach emits NEITHER event and\n48|  changes no Owner/Replica, lease, or fencing state; v1 readers retain v4\n49|  as inert immutable history and derive nothing.\n50|\n51|## Coverage ratio (measured, not planned)\n52|\n53|**60 of 60 AC rows driven** through production entries by named committed\n54|tests — matrix in `internal/termbind/TRACEABILITY.md`, reproduced with\n55|spec-clause mapping in `TASK-260830-2056mm_conformance-matrix.md`.\n56|Killer-presence check: 21 distinct killer tests referenced by the harness,\n57|all present (`go test -list`), none missing.\n58|\n59|## Mutants (shipped harness, per-plant raw logs)\n60|\n61|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/termbind/mutant_harness.py` —\n62|30 rows: 28 narrowing + 1 supplementary arm-delete (D-emit-noresolve,\n63|labeled) + 1 harmless SURVIVED control. Pass 1 and pass 2: **30/30 each**,\n64|plus two full plain-list runs, exit 0. Per-row verbose logs (raw go output\n65|+ subprocess exit) and verdict lists are in the evidence tarball;\n66|production blobs sha256-identical before/after every run (diff clean).\n67|No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source\n68|text (stated bound, harness executes the behavioral suite).\n69|Extended batteries re-run in this session: axpane 56/56 twice (3 new\n70|story-close rows verbose ×2), terminstance 122/122 twice (6 new rows\n71|verbose ×2), blobs restored.\n72|\n73|## Crash / idempotency\n74|\n75|Real SIGKILL seams (unix): `TestAttachCrashChildSelfTerminates`,\n76|`TestRecoverCreateAfterKillRecoversChild`; append-hook abort/replay\n77|`TestEmitAppendHookSeams`; byte-identical retry replay\n78|`TestEmitAppendsIdempotently`, `TestAttachIdenticalRetryReplays`.\n79|\n80|## Story-close items\n81|\n82|- Registry: `section:4.1` bound NEW (sliver 1/5) via `storyNewV070Bindings`\n83|  with literal matching + clause remeasurement; 4.B/4.D/5.2 upgraded\n84|  (slivers), 7.A upgraded (partial); seven new acceptance cases. NOTE: the\n85|  producer's \"§13.1\" recovery rule lives at §4.1 lines 1395/1399 in the\n86|  pinned v0.7.0 document; §13.1's eight measured clauses are\n87|  launch-plan/boot-direct/argv rules owned by another story, so\n88|  `section:13.1` is untouched.\n89|- Digest re-pinned by derivation (transient in-package probe calling\n90|  `decodeOwnershipRegistry` + `json.Marshal` + sha256, removed after):\n91|  `DERIVED-DIGEST: 89944b8c6ec75703c0e07432890182ebbb9bb405f28502b05a6632662cebee9b\n92|  (canonical bytes: 166083)` — equals the pin in `traceability.go`.\n93|- `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` GREEN:\n94|  `traceability ok: contracts=64 normative_sections=36 acceptance_cases=147\n95|  fixtures=33 compatibility_contracts=55 assigned_scopes=0`\n96|  `section coverage: bindings=69 full=2 partial=9 sliver=9 unevidenced=45\n97|  unmeasured=4 unowned=7 clauses_discharged=63/574`\n98|- Section-scoped measured ratios (quoted verbatim; exit 1 by design —\n99|  assigned-scope admission requires full, these bindings honestly carry\n100|  sliver/partial gap text): 4.1 → 1/5 sliver; 4.B → 1/12 sliver;\n101|  4.D → 1/3 sliver; 5.2 → 3/18 sliver; 7.A → 1/2 partial.\n102|- README: `termbind` leaf section with exact test commands, no CLI/capability\n103|  claims; \"Measured coverage of this repository\" updated to the printed\n104|  numbers (pin test green).\n105|- LOGBOOK: one newest-first story entry for TASK-260830-2056mm.\n106|- Inherited residuals CLOSED: axpane P3-1/P3-4/P3-5, terminstance P3-1..P3-4\n107|  (witnesses verbatim, mirror rows); P3-2/P3-3 stated as owner bounds.\n108|\n109|## Validation suite (30 configured commands)\n110|\n111|`cmd01-cmd30.log` (cmd05 split a–h) — all exit 0, in the evidence tarball.\n112|Accepted from already-attached logs: cmd01–cmd30. Reran myself in this\n113|session: full `tracecheck`, all five section-scoped runs, `go test\n114|./internal/termbind/`, all three mutant harnesses twice each with per-row\n115|verbose logs, the killer-presence ratio check, and the digest derivation.\n116|`task-board validate` exits 0 (reports pre-existing missing-activity issues\n117|on other elements, none on this task).\n118|\n119|## Rejection-pattern self-check\n120|\n121|(a) Literals asserted from spec text at entries (pinned codes, digests,\n122|bounds), not production constants. (b) Every rule driven through the entry\n123|the matrix names; dual Build/Decode sides each carry narrowing rows.\n124|(c) Landed owners composed (scalar UUIDv7, canonicaljson closed shapes,\n125|sessrepo/sessstate/sessquery, Registry.AdmitProbe, sessprofile) — only\n126|package-specific rules are new. (d) Inputs driven, effects asserted; no\n127|census stands in for behavior. (e) 28 narrowing rows + labeled arm-delete +\n128|applied SURVIVED control, one raw log per plant per run. (f) Every\n129|\"composes/never\" sentence is backed by a failing-without test or stated as\n130|an explicit bound (attach no-emit absence-by-construction, CLI Result 4\n131|tripwire, lease-authority adoption rows).","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cb41","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3fc-2962-7bc0-91c2-787ae4899fa1"},"sequence":1019,"recorded_at":1780531400002033,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a"},"call_id":"call_01a0b3ffefe370a49524c5f82bab310c","text":"Read text file `/tmp/tb2056/results-rev2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2056mm results rev2 — race-gate rework\n2|\n3|Rework run (RUN-260918-2c22a5) after autonomous recovery: rev1 CR validation\n4|stopped at command 5/30 (`go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m`, exit 1).\n5|Root cause was a single test-fixture data race; the fix is test-only and the\n6|rev1 deliverable is otherwise carried verbatim.\n7|\n8|Candidate: UNCOMMITTED working tree on branch\n9|`task-board/story/STORY-260830-ptxkqe` atop checkpoint ca1c1d9.\n10|No commit, rebase, or branch operation performed by this run.\n11|\n12|Trunk: origin/main == c3aae73 at handoff (verified `git fetch origin main`;\n13|merge-base == origin/main), so no `refresh-candidate` was needed.\n14|`task-board.config.json` is byte-identical to HEAD (verified\n15|`git diff HEAD --quiet -- task-board.config.json`). No validation command added.\n16|\n17|Normative source: SPEC.v0.7.0 (unchanged from rev1).\n18|\n19|## Root cause (evidence-backed)\n20|\n21|`TASK-260830-2056mm_change-request_rev1-validation.log` lines 708-853:\n22|`WARNING: DATA RACE` — goroutine 170 wrote `universe[extraID]` at\n23|`internal/termbind/resolve_test.go:172` while goroutine 169 read the same map\n24|in `mapUniverse.Lookup` (`fixtures_test.go:490`) via `ResolveEvidence`\n25|(`resolve.go:86`); a second identical race at `resolve_test.go:181`.\n26|`TestResolveEvidenceRequiresManifestAndProbe` built ONE `mapUniverse` and\n27|shared it across four `t.Parallel()` subtests while the two \"second\" cases\n28|extended it. The detector then failed the whole `termbind` package\n29|(fifteen tests reporting \"race detected during execution of test\"); every\n30|other package in the repo was green, including commands 1-4 of the suite.\n31|\n32|Audit of the rest of the package: every other parallel subtest already builds\n33|its own `universeMap(t, world)`; `TestResolveEvidenceShapeBounds` shares one\n34|map read-only (safe); `Registry.AdmitProbe` is safe for concurrent use\n35|(`Registry.Resolve` takes `mutex.RLock` and returns a clone,\n36|`internal/terminalbackend/terminalbackend.go:519`). No production code races:\n37|no production byte changed.\n38|\n39|## Fix\n40|\n41|`internal/termbind/resolve_test.go`, `TestResolveEvidenceRequiresManifestAndProbe`:\n42|each of the four parallel subtests now builds its own `universeMap(t, world)`\n43|copy before resolving; the mutating cases extend only their own copy.\n44|Same assertions, same killer names, same behavior.\n45|\n46|Whole-tree proof: reconstructed the rev1 candidate\n47|(`git archive c3aae73` + apply `..._change-request_rev1.patch`, which is the\n48|whole-story patch against trunk) and diffed recursively against this worktree.\n49|Exactly two files differ — the fix hunk plus this run's LOGBOOK entry:\n50|\n51|- `internal/termbind/resolve_test.go` (the fix, +7/-1 lines)\n52|- `LOGBOOK.md` (rev2 entry, purely additive)\n53|\n54|Full diff in the evidence tarball as `rev1-to-rev2.diff`. No production file,\n55|no other test, no registry/README/traceability byte differs from rev1.\n56|\n57|## Verification (this run)\n58|\n59|Reran myself (logs in `TASK-260830-2056mm_producer-evidence-rev2.tar.gz`):\n60|\n61|- `go test ./internal/termbind/ -race -count=10` → ok, exit 0 (plus two\n62|  further `-count=3` passes, one saved as `termbind-race-count3.log`)\n63|- `go test ./internal/axpane/ ./internal/terminstance/ -race -count=1` → ok/ok\n64|  (`siblings-race.log`)\n65|- `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/termbind/mutant_harness.py` →\n66|  30/30 on pass 1 and pass 2, verdict lists byte-identical\n67|  (`termbind-harness-pass1.log`, `termbind-harness-pass2.log`); targeted\n68|  verbose row `N-resolve-manifest-count` (whose killer is the edited test)\n69|  still KILLED (`targeted-row-verbose.log`)\n70|- `gofmt -l` clean, `go vet ./internal/termbind/` ok, `go build ./...` ok,\n71|  config byte-identical, trunk pinned (`gates.log`)\n72|- No `__pycache__` under the worktree (`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` throughout)\n73|\n74|Accepted from already-attached rev1 evidence (bytes unchanged, so results\n75|carry): commands 1-4 and 6-30 of the configured suite, per-plant verbose\n76|mutant logs, crash/idempotency logs, tracecheck section runs, digest\n77|derivation. The full 30-command suite reruns automatically at handoff.\n78|\n79|## Coverage and story-close (carried from rev1, unchanged)\n80|\n81|- 60 of 60 AC rows driven through production entries by named committed\n82|  tests — no test added, removed, or renamed, so\n83|  `TASK-260830-2056mm_conformance-matrix.md` (rev1) and\n84|  `internal/termbind/TRACEABILITY.md` stand without modification.\n85|- Mutants: 28 narrowing + 1 labeled supplementary arm-delete + 1 harmless\n86|  SURVIVED control, 30/30 twice (re-run above against the fixed tree).\n87|- Registry `ownership.v0.7.0.json`, re-pinned digest, tracecheck numbers,\n88|  README section, and the seven new acceptance cases are byte-identical to\n89|  rev1; nothing re-derived because nothing they measure changed.\n90|\n91|## Rejection-pattern self-check (delta)\n92|\n93|(a) No expectation touched. (b) The edited killer still drives the composed\n94|entry (`ResolveEvidence`, production call site `resolve.go:86` lookup path)\n95|and still kills `N-resolve-manifest-count` — verified, not assumed.\n96|(c) No landed gate touched. (d) No census added. (e) Full harness re-run\n97|twice with identical verdicts, plus the verbose per-plant log for the row\n98|whose killer changed. (f) \"No production byte changed\" is the measured\n99|whole-tree diff, quoted above. Reported ratio (60/60) is rev1's measured\n100|ratio on unchanged tests, not a new claim.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
