{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e4b7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3fc-2962-7bc0-91c2-787ae4899fa1"},"sequence":4278,"recorded_at":1780531400008551,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6cf4561a-8326-47da-a916-4850b6a43e2a"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Ready for review — handed off to review (revision 3 construction triggered).\n\n## What was done\n\nReworked the rev2 review findings (no P1; P2-1 + five P3) in the Story worktree, candidate left uncommitted on `task-board/story/STORY-260830-ptxkqe` at checkpoint `ca1c1d9`:\n\n- **P2-1 (Binding parser):** `ParseTerminalBinding` now enforces `protocol_version` major 1 and `extensions == {}` per the §4.B table, and `bindingIdentity` refuses JSON numbers at any depth plus nested duplicate members before the JCS transform (strict UseNumber decode mirroring the landed terminalbackend rule). Every member arm is driven negatively through the entry (37-subtest battery, code+detail pinned), with verdict-agreement batteries against the landed rules and 6 new narrowing harness rows.\n- **P3-1:** pre-scan harness notes, wrapper docs, README bootstrap sentence corrected to the documented redundancy; LOGBOOK F2 correction appended.\n- **P3-2:** `EmitResumed` checkpoint/pair binding stated explicitly as a caller bound with a boundary-pinning test.\n- **P3-3:** generation-bound-before-read witness committed with its harness row.\n- **P3-4:** row 57 / 5.2#18 restated as a bound, descriptor test added to the identity-exact case, `resolve.go` doc scoped, README corrected.\n- **P3-5:** restore/terminate-stale deferred to a Story follow-up task; `HandoffFailed` non-applicability recorded.\n- **Story-close:** registry edited (5.2 gap + 8 test citations with mirror updates), digest re-derived `b09b5b9f…` (canonical bytes 167094), tracecheck green `63/574` with identical section ratios.\n\n## Evidence (measured)\n\n- AC: **65 of 66 rows driven** (row 57 stated bound); all 60 package tests PASS, coverage 83.7%\n- Mutants: termbind **36/36 twice** (34 narrowing + arm-delete + SURVIVED control, verdicts identical, blobs identical); axpane 56/56, terminstance 122/122\n- Full suite 41/41, race gate 41/41 with 0 DATA RACE (4 bounded chunks), gofmt/vet/build/cross-builds/cataloggen/task-board-validate all green\n- Attached: `TASK-260830-2056mm_results-rev3.md` (finding-by-finding table), `TASK-260830-2056mm_conformance-matrix-rev3.md`, `TASK-260830-2056mm_producer-evidence-rev3.tar.gz` (real gzip, 97 entries, per-plant raw logs)\n\nOne honest note: the `N-binding-members` narrowing survived once mid-run because the new number walk masks a numeric extra member; the killer was re-isolated to a string extra (code+detail pinned) and the row kills. Trunk stayed `c3aae73`, no refresh needed; `task-board.config.json` byte-identical.","reason":null}}
